<title>SINGAPORE: Vickers Ballas 1996 net leaps 41 pct.</title>
<headline>Vickers Ballas 1996 net leaps 41 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    48.55  vs   34.41</p>
<p>Dividend (cents)		     5.00  vs    5.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   20.00  vs   14.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			     234.54  vs  185.82</p>
<p>Other income incl. interest     65.27  vs   39.38</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  28.49  vs   12.94</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    4.18   vs    4.64</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     63.73   vs   47.03</p>
<p>    Tax				    15.56   vs   12.30</p>
<p>    Minorities			    0.17   vs    0.02</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		     0.00   vs    2.24 (gain)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: July 21, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: July 7, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Vickers Ballas Holdings Ltd, a stockbroking firm, said the Singapore stock market had performed less favourably in 1996, but its results had benefitted from the performance of the regional stock markets it operates in.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
